```
Title: Suspicious WSL Binary Hijack via Proxy Execution
Author: Swachchhanda Shrawan Poudel (Nextron Systems)
Date: 2026-05-05
Level: high
Description: Detects C:\Windows\System32\wsl.exe spawning a child wsl.exe process from outside the legitimate WSL install locations.
 When WSL or bash is invoked, the System32 stub (wsl.exe) looks up the InstallLocation registry key and executes the wsl.exe found there.
 An attacker who modifies InstallLocation to a controlled path causes the stub to transparently proxy execution to a malicious payload,
 which then appears as a wsl.exe child of the legitimate System32 stub.
MITRE Tactic: Uncategorized
Tags: attack.stealth, attack.t1036.005, attack.t1218
Reference: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/master/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_wsl_binary_hijack_execution.yml
 False Positives:
   - Unlikely
```
Image="*\\wsl.exe" ParentImage="C:\\Windows\\System32\\wsl.exe" NOT (Image IN ("C:\\Windows\\System32\\wsl.exe", "C:\\Program Files\\WSL\\wsl.exe") OR Image IN ("C:\\Windows\\WinSxS\\amd64_microsoft-windows-lxss-wsl_*", "C:\\Windows\\WinSxS\\arm64_microsoft-windows-lxss-wsl_*", "C:\\Program Files\\WindowsApps\\MicrosoftCorporationII.WindowsSubsystemForLinux*") OR (Image="*\\AppData\\Local\\Microsoft\\WindowsApps\\*" Image="C:\\Users\\*"))